    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0552" n="470" xml:id="pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1401.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the embassy’s note of
                    the 8th instant, regarding the receipt of ammunition at Ojinaga by Gen. Luque, I
                    have the honor to inclose for your information and consideration a copy of a
                    letter from the Assistant Attorney General,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d674-f1"/>
                    stating that the matter will be given attention and suggesting that his
                    department be advised in advance of future shipments of the kind mentioned.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
